DESCRIPTION:IEB Grade 12 - Java - Access - Other four-term independent scho
 ol (ISASA guideline) - T1 W1\n\nProgramming:\n- Java 31 (part): The PAT - I
 EB\n    focus: the PAT documents: specification\, design\, and technical an
 d testing\; comments in the project: what each method does\, receives and g
 ives back\n    https://itcoder.co.za/lesson.php?c=java&id=patieb\n- Java 16
  (part): Arrays - remembering a whole list\n    focus: two-dimensional arra
 ys: rows\, columns and their totals\n    https://itcoder.co.za/lesson.php?c
 =java&id=lesson16\n\nTheory:\n- What makes a computer fast\n    https://itc
 oder.co.za/lesson.php?c=theory12&id=performance\n\nDatabases:\n- SQL 3: Key
 s and relationships\n    focus: keys: primary\, foreign\, composite\; relat
 ionships one-to-one\, one-to-many\, many-to-many\; referential integrity\n 
    https://itcoder.co.za/lesson.php?c=sql&id=dbkeys\n- SQL 4: A good design
 \n    focus: redundancy\, repeating groups\, duplicate and derived data\, a
 tomic and non-atomic fields\; update\, insert and delete anomalies\n    htt
 ps://itcoder.co.za/lesson.php?c=sql&id=dbdesign
